<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were largely unchanged on Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Only the six-month rate was a shade lower.</p>
<p>Traders said the PHIBOR merely mirrored the overnight money market which had also been steady on absence of new factors.</p>
<p>They said banks were flush with pesos as they continued to stay away from term reverse repos due to the 20 percent tax.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  FEB 18		 FEB 17</p>
<p>    1 W		9 15/16		 9 15/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9 15/16		 9 15/16</p>
<p>    1 M	     10  1/16		10  1/16</p>
<p>    2 M	     10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M	     10  3/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    6 M	     10  5/16		10  3/8</p>
<p>    12M	     10  9/16		10  9/16</p>
<p>    VAL	     19-Feb		  18-Feb</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
